{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5ea34fe8-9420-41ba-a6ee-0bcd0395daad",
    "name": "HaderApp - security demo (Group 40)",
    "description": "Security scenarios for the demo video and report (section 12).\n\n1. Fill in the variables (Variables tab): supabasePublishableKey (from shared/config.js), and each account's email + password. Put passwords in CURRENT value only, so they are never exported or committed.\n2. Run the '0. Setup' folder once.\n3. Click through folders 1-6 in order (6, the rate limit, uses up the minute's verify allowance, so it goes last); every request has a test showing the expected status code.\n\nNothing here changes data: refused requests are refused before any write, and the only allowed requests are reads.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup - run once before recording",
      "description": "Logs in each account through Supabase Auth and saves the tokens into collection variables (nothing to paste). Then finds the attendee's certificate to test against.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Log in: attendee",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "apikey",
                "value": "{{supabasePublishableKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{attendeeEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{attendeePassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Attendee who owns a certificate."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('attendeeToken', pm.response.json().access_token);",
                  "console.log('attendeeToken saved');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in: second attendee",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "apikey",
                "value": "{{supabasePublishableKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{attendee2Email}}\", \"password\": \"{{attendee2Password}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "A different attendee (does NOT own the certificate)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('attendee2Token', pm.response.json().access_token);",
                  "console.log('attendee2Token saved');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in: organizer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "apikey",
                "value": "{{supabasePublishableKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{organizerEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{organizerPassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "An organizer who does NOT organize the certificate's workshop (otherwise test 3.2 returns 200). Use a different organizer for the end-to-end part of the video."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('organizerToken', pm.response.json().access_token);",
                  "console.log('organizerToken saved');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in: user with no role",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "apikey",
                "value": "{{supabasePublishableKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{noRoleEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{noRolePassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Account with no profile/role."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('noRoleToken', pm.response.json().access_token);",
                  "console.log('noRoleToken saved');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Find the attendee's certificate",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{attendeeToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{certUrl}}/certificates/me",
            "description": "Saves certId, verifyCode and certWorkshopId of the attendee's newest certificate that is not revoked."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const c = (pm.response.json().certificates || []).find(x => !x.revoked_at);",
                  "pm.test('attendee has a valid certificate', () => pm.expect(c, 'generate one in the app first').to.be.ok);",
                  "if (c) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('certId', c.certificate_id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('verifyCode', c.verification_code);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('certWorkshopId', String(c.workshop_id));",
                  "  console.log('Using certificate', c.certificate_id, 'workshop', c.workshop_id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Login required (401)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "No token: my certificates",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{certUrl}}/certificates/me",
            "description": "Protected route with no Authorization header."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Forged token (signature changed)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{certUrl}}/certificates/me",
            "description": "A real token whose signature was altered. The backend checks it against Supabase's public keys and rejects it."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const p = pm.collectionVariables.get('attendeeToken').split('.');",
                  "const forged = `${p[0]}.${p[1]}.${p[2].slice(0, -6)}AAAAAA`;",
                  "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: `Bearer ${forged}` });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Garbage token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer not-a-real-token"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{certUrl}}/certificates/me",
            "description": "Not a JWT at all."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
